/* time complexity - O(n)  each node processed once
space complexity - o(1)
INTUITION
Use two pointers:

sp = slow → moves 1 step

fp = fast → moves 2 steps

If the fast pointer reaches null, it means the list ended → no cycle.

If the list has a cycle, the fast pointer eventually “laps” the slow pointer because it moves faster.

When fast and slow meet, it confirms a cycle exists.

Return true if they meet, else false.
*/


class Solution {
    public boolean hasCycle(ListNode head) {
        ListNode fp = head;
        ListNode sp = head;
        while(fp!=null && fp.next!=null){
            fp = fp.next.next;
            sp = sp.next;
            if(fp==sp)return true;
        }
        
        return false;
    }
}
